# Description

DPA-3.3-1M is trained using a multitask strategy on the [OpenLAM datasets V2](https://www.aissquare.com/datasets/detail?pageType=datasets&name=OpenLAM-TrainingSet-v2&id=391) with ***modification***. Compared with DPA-3.2-5M, the following changes were made:

1. The model depth was decreased from 24 layers to 6 layers for efficiency.
2. Two new datasets were added to improve model performance in the domain of catalysis. Namely, the [CLAM dataset](https://doi.org/10.1021/jacsau.5c01112) and the [OC20mAds dataset](https://fair-chem.github.io/oc20-mads/)
3. The parameterization of spin multiplicity and charge were decoupled from the fitting net and used as explicit inputs during embedding construction.

